		{
			dependencies: ["7E20000000000001"]
			description: [
				"Thermal's generators are called &eDynamos&r, and there are five: Stirling (solid fuel), Compression (liquid fuel), Magmatic (lava), Numismatic (coins and gems) and Lapidary (gems)."
				""
				"&e&lThey all take the same augments&r, which is the point of Thermal - one upgrade system across every machine and dynamo."
				""
				"&7Fuel Catalysts make fuel last longer; Boost augments raise output at the cost of efficiency. Pick per dynamo depending on whether fuel or throughput is your constraint.&r"
				""
				"&8The Magmatic Dynamo pairs with your Cyclic Melter loop - infinite cobble to lava to power."
			]
			icon: "thermal:dynamo_stirling"
			id: "9200000000000001"
			rewards: [{
				id: "9200A00000000001"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Thermal's generators"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "9200B00000000100"
					item: "thermal:dynamo_stirling"
					type: "item"
				}
			]
			title: "&6Dynamos"
			x: -8.0d
			y: 3.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["9200000000000001"]
			description: [
				"&eAugments&r slot into every Thermal machine and dynamo, and they are what makes the mod worth using."
				""
				"&e&lThe main families:&r"
				"&7- &fUpgrade&7 - raises the machine's whole tier at once"
				"&7- &fSpeed / Efficiency&7 - the usual trade"
				"&7- &fAuxiliary&7 - machine-specific extras like extra output chance"
				"&7- &fFluid / Item tank&7 - bigger internal buffers"
				""
				"&c&lAugment slots are limited by machine tier&r, so an Upgrade augment often pays for itself by unlocking more slots."
				""
				"&7Because it is one system, anything you learn on a Pulverizer applies to every other Thermal block you ever place.&r"
			]
			icon: "thermal:machine_crafter"
			id: "9200000000000002"
			rewards: [{
				id: "9200A00000000002"
				type: "xp"
				xp: 30
			}]
			subtitle: "&7One upgrade system, every machine"
			tasks: [
